description: List rendering, virtualization and scrolling performance guidelines for React Native projects
alwaysApply: false
---

# Lists

- Prefer `LegendList` or `FlashList` over `FlatList` for large or performance-sensitive lists
- Use `FlatList` only for simple and lightweight lists
- Provide stable and unique keys for items
- Avoid nested virtualized lists when possible
- Prefer pagination and virtualization for large datasets
- Use pull-to-refresh when the screen requires data refresh
- Avoid expensive calculations inside `renderItem`
- Avoid inline `renderItem` functions when possible
- Prefer memoized list items for large datasets
- Use estimated item sizes when supported
- Keep scrolling smooth and responsive
